WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.430
ELIAS PINTO: Oh,
hey there, Nick.

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.540
NICK PAN: Hey, Elias.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.160
Fancy seeing you here.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.610
ELIAS PINTO: I don't often
see you down these parts.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.380
Now, where's that
old boat of yours?

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.070
NICK PAN: It's that
beaut over there.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.830
The one with that
light blue spinnaker.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.450
ELIAS PINTO: Spinnaker you say?

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.440
Now, what's that?

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.390
Is that one of those
whiz bang new gizmos

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.840
I should be knowing more about?

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.180
NICK PAN: A spinnaker?

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.860
And you call yourself a sailor?

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.956
You old buccaneer.

00:00:24.956 --> 00:00:28.220
A spinnaker is the
front sail of your boat.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.550
You know what else it is?

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:30.300
ELIAS PINTO: What?

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.110
NICK PAN: Spinnaker
is an open source,

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.290
multi-cloud, continuous
delivery platform

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.480
for releasing software
changes with high velocity

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.340
and confidence.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.280
Let's jump to a demo.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:47.550
So this is the
Spinnaker dashboard.

00:00:47.550 --> 00:00:49.910
And on this dashboard, you're
able to see the resources

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.650
that Spinnaker manages.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.990
In this case, we're managing
resources on Google Cloud

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:55.550
platform, and we're
actually going

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.520
to exhibit a demo, which
is a developer pushing code

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.370
into a release branch, having
that release branch be built,

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.970
tested, validated, and then
promoted into production,

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.840
and then deployed
into production.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.950
So as we see here, we
have two load balancers--

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:12.520
an ingress load balancer
for a staging environment,

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:14.090
as well as an
ingress load balancer

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:16.370
for a production environment.

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:19.070
Both of these are hooked up
to Google Kubernetes engine

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:20.960
clusters, and you'll
see here they're

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.260
both wearing the
same Go application

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.890
with a white background
just exhibiting

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.764
the text "hello world."

00:01:26.764 --> 00:01:29.180
So let's say I'm a developer
and want to release a feature

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:30.749
change to this application.

00:01:30.749 --> 00:01:33.290
In this case, we're just going
to change the background color

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.990
from white to yellow, and
to do this I would just

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.360
jump to my source code.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.470
I go ahead and adjust
the index at HTML

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:45.350
file to go from white to yellow,
or in this case, light yellow.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:49.130
And then I would just push this
commit into my version control.

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:51.361
For this case, I'm using GitHub.

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:53.360
So we just go through the
standard get commands,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.901
and we add a commit
to say that we're

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:58.310
adjusting to light yellow.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:02:00.950
And then once we actually
push that into our codebase,

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:02.780
we're able to kick
off our CI/CD,

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.450
or Continuous Integration
Continuous Deployment,

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:07.230
pipeline.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.070
So I'll just go ahead and log in
to GitHub, and then from here,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:13.590
we'll kick off that process.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.130
So if I hover back into the
actual Google Cloud Platform

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:19.100
console, you'll see here that
we have a tool known as Google

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.170
Cloud Source Repositories.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.730
And what this tool
does is allows

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:24.590
you to mirror
GitHub repositories

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:27.890
within Google Cloud backed
by reliable, durable object

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.037
storage.

00:02:29.037 --> 00:02:30.620
If you see here,
we've already noticed

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.300
that commit that I
pushed into GitHub,

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:33.675
and you'll see
that commit adjust

00:02:33.675 --> 00:02:35.370
to light yellow background.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.450
And here this is being
noticed almost in real time.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.440
From here, we have
a container registry

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.650
build trigger that's
basically monitoring

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:48.080
that cloud repository and
building a container, which

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.600
will be our docker artifact
that will then deploy

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.370
into the Kubernetes cluster.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.220
So you'll see here
there's a trigger that's

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:56.800
monitoring our GitHub repo.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.740
So we have created
this docker image.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.020
It's been built just now.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:06.640
It's 288 megabytes in size, and
we've tagged it with two tags--

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.680
one, latest; and
the other one, MD5

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.680
hash digest of the commit ID.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.800
So this is where
Spinnaker comes in.

00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.112
What Spinnaker does is that
it monitors a docker registry,

00:03:17.112 --> 00:03:18.570
and when there's
a new image that's

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:22.210
uploaded to that registry,
it'll kick off a pipeline.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:23.770
So I hit the Refresh button.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.160
We should see a pipeline
for deploying to stage

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:27.430
that's about to be run.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:29.850
So you'll see here,
it's now running.

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.580
So at this stage, what it
does, if you see over here,

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.080
it's monitoring
that docker registry

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.820
or that Google
Container Registry

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:38.730
to see when an image is
actually uploaded there.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.770
Once it detects an
image has been uploaded,

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.907
it then begins the
deployment process.

00:03:42.907 --> 00:03:44.490
So here you can see
we're deploying it

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.520
to our staging environment
using a red/black deployment

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.940
strategy.

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:50.904
So this takes some
time to complete.

00:03:50.904 --> 00:03:52.320
We're going to
take a quick break,

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.350
and I'll come back
once it's completed.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:57.590
All right, and we're back.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.330
You can see that that deployed
a stage step completed,

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:02.730
and now we're held up
at this validate stage.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.184
What's awesome
about Spinnaker is

00:04:04.184 --> 00:04:06.600
that it gives you the ability
to have a human intervention

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.810
in your pipeline.

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.570
So you have the
manual judgment step,

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.640
which allows you to
approve this pipeline

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.230
and move on to
the next step when

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.730
you've confirmed
that you're staging

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.220
environment looks good to go.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.970
So I'll go back to
our cluster side.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.870
We'll click on that ingress
load balancer, find that IP,

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.530
and I still have that
opened in my tab.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.080
So I'll go to my top
right and check this page.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:26.520
When I refresh
this, it does show

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:28.270
that we've made that
change, and it is now

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.069
a light yellow background.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.860
If we looked at the
production environment,

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.080
we'll see that's still
showing a white background.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.800
So we'll say this is good to go.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:39.070
We'll hit Continue and now
basically go to the next step.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.710
We have confirmed that we've
validated that the release

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:43.680
stage is good to
go, and now we're

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.670
at the point where we're
comfortable to promote

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.061
to production.

00:04:47.061 --> 00:04:48.810
So in this promote to
production pipeline,

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.680
we have numerous steps.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.900
And this also takes
some time to complete

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.180
but ensures we are able
to do a reliable as well

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.667
as a repeatable deployment.

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.000
So I'm going to pause the video.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.640
We're going to come back
once it's completed.

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:01.640
And there we have it.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.010
The promote to production
stage has completed.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:06.080
At this point we should
have that pristine docker

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:09.050
image deployed into our
production Kubernetes

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.010
environment.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.240
So we go back to that
ingress load balancer.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.464
I still have that tab
open with that IP.

00:05:14.464 --> 00:05:16.130
At the moment, it's
still showing white,

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:19.070
but when I hit Refresh, it
should go to light yellow.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.130
There you go.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.060
So at this point, we've done
an end-to-end CI/CD deployment

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:25.520
from source code
into build steps,

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:27.730
released into a
staging environment,

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.450
and then promoted
into production.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.504
And Spinnaker is what
makes this all possible.

00:05:31.504 --> 00:05:33.170
ELIAS PINTO: I thought
I knew everything

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:35.900
about sailing and GCP.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.129
But boy, I was wrong.

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:39.545
If you're working
on cool projects

00:05:39.545 --> 00:05:41.270
and you want to get
in touch with us,

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:43.710
click on the link
below to contact us.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.310
Till next time.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:49.660
